# Build context is the REPOSITORY ROOT (both Dockerfiles need `shared/`, which
# resolves outside their own directory). Everything the two backend images do
# not need must be excluded here, or it is uploaded to the daemon on every build
# and, worse, can end up inside the image.
#
# The measured reason this file exists: `api/demo/media` is **2.1 GB** of cached
# stock video. `api.Dockerfile` copies `api/demo` so the dataset tooling ships
# with the image, and without the exclusion below that copy takes the media with
# it — onto a 30 GB VM disk, through a build context uploaded over the network.
# The seed is run from a developer machine anyway (see docs/deployment), so the
# media is never needed on the server.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
# Nothing carrying a credential may enter the build context. `.env.example`
# files are templates with empty values and are deliberately kept.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
deploy/.env
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.production
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
id_rsa*

# ------------------------------------------------------------- dependencies
# Reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile. Copying a host tree in would
# also bring native binaries built for the wrong platform — the usual cause of
# "Could not load the sharp module" or an FFmpeg binding that will not link.
**/node_modules

# ------------------------------------------------------------ build output
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/coverage
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ------------------------------------------------ apps this image never builds
# The build context is the repository ROOT (both Dockerfiles need `shared/`,
# which resolves outside their own directory), so Docker uploads everything not
# excluded here — including the two Next.js apps, which neither backend image
# copies. Measured with build artefacts present: user/ 3.4 GB, admin/ 1.5 GB.
# They are Vercel projects and have no business in a backend image, nor in the
# tarball sent to the daemon over the network.
user
admin

# --------------------------------------------------------- the 2.1 GB reason
# Cached stock media for the demo dataset. The seeder runs from a developer
# machine against the production API, so the server never reads these bytes.
api/demo/media

# ------------------------------------------------------- runtime/local state
# Uploaded and processed media on a disk-storage deployment, plus resumable
# upload chunks. These are volumes at runtime and must never be baked in.
file-server/public
file-server/temp
file-server/storage
api/public/uploads

# ------------------------------------------------------------- repo furniture
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.agents
.code-review-graph
.mcp.json
output
docs
**/*.md
!**/README.md

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- logs
**/*.log
**/logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- tests
# Not run inside the image; the CI/local gate covers them.
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
**/*.test.ts
**/__tests__
**/browser-verify
**/playwright-report
**/test-results

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- deploy self
# The images do not build themselves, and the Worker is deployed by wrangler.
deploy/r2-worker
deploy/docker-compose.yml
deploy/nginx
deploy/gce
